    "PREAMBLE": "Rahul Chhahar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 February,\n2023\nAuthor: Dinesh Kumar Paliwal\nBench: Dinesh Kumar Paliwal\n1  IN THE HIGH COURT OF MADHYA PRADESH  AT JABALPUR  BEFORE  HON'BLE SHRI JUSTICE DINESH KUMAR PALIWAL  ON THE 20 th OF FEBRUARY, 2023  MISC. CRIMINAL CASE No. 23202 of 2022\nBETWEEN:-\n ARCHANA JAISWAL W/O SHRI DEVENDRA JAISWAL,\n AGED ABOUT 32 YEARS, OCCUPATION:\nHOUSE WIFE  R/O C-53, KARCHUN, SOMYA ATLANTIC KATARA HILLS,\n DISTT. BHOPAL (MP) (MADHYA PRADESH)\n.....APPL  (BY SHRI MANISH TIWARI-ADVOCATE )\n AND  THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH POLICE  STATION MP NAGAR DISTRICT BHOPAL M.P. (MADHYA  PRADESH)\n .....RESPOND  (BY SHRI PRADEEP GUPTA-GOVERNMENT ADVOCATE )\nMISC . CRIMINAL CASE No. 56851 of 2022\nBETWEEN:-\n RAHUL CHHAHAR S/O LATE KISHAN CHHAHAR, AGED  ABOUT 33 YEARS, OCCUPATION:\nPRIVATE JOB 101 D-\nSECTOR BANJARI KOLAR ROAD BHOPAL DISTRICT\nBHOPAL M.P. (MADHYA PRADESH)\n.....APPL  (BY SHRI PRAKAHR NAVERIA-ADVOCATE )\n AND  THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH POLICE  STATION M.P. NAGAR BHOPAL DISTRICT BHOPAL M.P.\n (MADHYA PRADESH)\n .....RESPOND Signature Not Verified Rahul Chhahar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 February, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/121408404/\n1\nSigned by: KUNDAN SHARMA Signing time: 2/24/2023 7:39:49 PM\n2  (BY SHRI PRADEEP GUPTA-ADVOCATE )\n MISC. CRIMINAL CASE No. 1086 of 2023  BETWEEN:-\n MUKESH KUMAR PAWAR S/O SHRI HARI KUMAR,\n AGED ABOUT 40 YEARS, OCCUPATION:\nSELF  EMPLOYEE H.NO.603 GREEN ACRES LALGHATI\nBHOPAL DISTRICT BHOPAL (MADHYA PRADESH)\n \n (BY SHRI ANKIT SAXENA-ADVOCATE)\nAND  THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH POLICE  STATION M.P. NAGAR DISTRICT BHOPAL (MADHYA  PRADESH)\n ..\n (BY SHRI PRADEEP GUPTA-GOVERNMENT ADVOCATE )\n These applications coming on for admission this day, th  the following:\n ORDER\n",
    "facts": "As per the prosecution case, the applicant and co-accused persons who were the director, managing director and employee/agents of the A.D.C. India Fishery Trading Company Pvt. Ltd. through their employee/agent collected huge amount from innocent persons assuring them to double their money Rahul Chhahar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 February, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/121408404/\n2 within a stipulated period.\nOn the other hand, they closed down the company office and embezzled crores of rupees of the investors.\nThus, they cheated innocent people.\n",
    "arguments": "Devendra Jaiswal has moved an application under Section 13-B of the Hindu Marriage Act against her before the Family Court Bhopal and same is pending.\nHe has been implicated only because he was the employee of the company.\nCompany has embezzled crores of rupees from the innocent investors.\nTherefore, no case is made out to release Rahul Chhahar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 20 February, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/121408404/\n3 her on bail.\nHe was actively associated with the operation of the company as proprietor of the company.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "Such prayer is not worth acceptance as while considering the second bail application High Court is not expected to appreciate the evidence of witnesses examined before the trial Court as it is for the trial Court to appreciate the reliability and truthfulness of the evidence of the prosecution witnesses.\nShe is wife of Devendra Jaiswal.\nShe has actively participated in the operation of the company.\nIn the case in hand, it cannot be overlooked that applicants in conspiracy and in connivance with co-accused Devendra Jaiswal and other co-accused persons played serious fraud upon innocent investors and deprived them of their hard earned money.\nApplicants also induced the innocent people to deposit the money with the company.\nTherefore, without expressing any opinion on the merit of the case but having taken into consideration all the facts and circumstances of the case, I am of the view that it is not a fit case for grant of bail.\n",
    "decision": "Therefore, these bail applications filed on behalf of applicants-Archana Jaiswal,\nRahul Chahar and Mukesh Kumar are dismissed.\n"
